date: 2025-06-16T00:00:00-04:00
---

Star 221,325 is a [[Joker World]] 221,325 worlds starward of Færrin prime. A [[Org/The Scale/index|Scale]] scouting party found it while searching the [[Infinite Horizon]] for places of interest, drawn by a magical presence and by slip-shielding over part of the surface.

An indigo rain falls here without pause. Where Færrin prime would show grassland south of Calaria, the ground is broken into leaning plateaus and canyons, and the rain soaks in rather than flooding, leaving the footing soft and slow. Toward the middle of a wide crater the plateaus tilt inward, and greenish-blue fire shows there, the only steady light under the rain. Lines run across the canyon walls where falling rain hisses away the moment it lands. The lines have no visible source and grow denser nearer the center. The cracks are where the world's creatures come from: [[Bestiary/Fiends|Hellions]] climb out of them by the horde. A crack can split open under a climber's hand, blasting sulfurous steam, with a small trident jabbing out of the fire.

In the last mile of the canyons, a traveler may hear a thought in their own voice, asking whether the work is worth it and how far they are willing to go.

At the center stands a sealed structure built of some combination of metal and vine, with a single door. The door shapes a question out of metal and vine, asking whether those before it would descend to save a soul tormented by captors, and it opens to those who answer yes. The building within is [[Geography/The Quorum|the Quorum]]. Some of the Scale's scouting party died crossing the chasms, and none of them were found afterward. The Scale's four delving specialists, Cliff Vandertrip, Manuel de la Cruzada, Zangron Lee and Gregor, have fought their way through the Hellions to the Quorum and been let in.
